  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised.<br />Statement II : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>MnCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>FeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are paramagnetic and have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> unpaired electrons, respectively.&nbsp;</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
